Wipe: This one is dedicated to 26th President of the United States Theodore Roosevelt, who was born on this day 168 years ago. I have visited more Theodore Roosevelt sites than most other presidents, having visited his birthplace in Manhattan, Inauguration Site in Buffalo, Home in Oyster Bay, and Gravesite in Oyster Bag aswell. The only thing I’m missing is his presidential library, which unfortunately is in North Dakota, because I can’t imagine I will be there anytime soon. Theodore Roosevelt was actually the first president gravesite I’ve seen and can remember (allegedly I went to the Ulysses S. Grant one many many years ago, but the visit I remember was one day after my visit to the Theodore Roosevelt one), and have since seen 17 more president gravesites. 7/10','#ff3a00','American University Centennial 422/424 Bathroom',3,NULL,7135444,4140642);

