I don''t even know what I''m doing half the time, honestly, like I''ll walk into a room and just stand there for a second because I forgot why I went in there, and then I''ll leave and remember three hours later while I''m doing something completely unrelated, which is kind of weird if you think about it, but I guess everything is weird if you think about it long enough, and sometimes I wonder why socks disappear in the dryer, even though I know there''s probably a normal explanation for it, but still, where do they go? Anyway, I was looking out the window earlier and there was a bird sitting on something, I couldn''t tell what it was sitting on, but it was there, just sitting, doing bird things, I guess, and then it flew away, which is probably what birds do most of the time, and now that I think about it, I haven''t had a really good sandwich in a while, or maybe I have and just forgot about it, because memory is weird like that, and the other day I heard a noise that sounded kind of like a microwave but it wasn''t a microwave, at least I don''t think it was, and I never figured out what it was, but that''s fine because not everything needs an explanation, sometimes things just happen and you move on, like when you drop a pencil and it rolls under the couch and you decide that pencil belongs to the couch now, which is probably a terrible way to treat your belongings, but whatever, it''s a pencil, and pencils are replaceable, unlike some things, like that one hoodie you had that was somehow perfect even though it was probably just a regular hoodie, and now it''s gone, and you can''t even remember where you last saw it, but anyway, I think it''s supposed to rain sometime soon, or maybe that was yesterday, I haven''t really been keeping track, and honestly, I don''t think the clouds are keeping track either, they''re just kind of floating around up there, doing whatever clouds do, which is probably nothing in particular, and I respect that, because sometimes I feel like doing absolutely nothing too, just sitting somewhere and letting time pass without having to accomplish anything, although then I''d probably get hungry, and once I got hungry I''d have to figure out what to eat, and that would turn into a whole thing, so maybe I''ll just keep sitting here for a little while longer and see what happens, because there''s really no reason to rush, and I think I left a light on somewhere.


