INSERT INTO "poop" VALUES(252615257,'2026-10-31T01:30:00.000Z',36.280544794734134,-80.359881296753883,0,'This particular case felt normal. Everything went accordingly smoothly. A hefty length of sweet time was given to the restroom today, as I responded to fellow homosapiens via a plethoria of social media platforms, utilizing my mobile device to do so. As I gradually type this out on top of my cushion of slumber, I question Self perception, it''s measurable influence on actions and behavior, not only exclusive to differing choices dependent on biological traits on the individual level, but for the difference in how we treat others based on our subjective, and partly intrinsic, socially, culturally, instinctually conditioned predisposed interpretations and assesments of physical characteristics, qualities, attributes, and its inherent effects on the overall success ratio of interactions, how, and what role they play in one''s life. To what degree does it have an influence? Height, posture, body language, voice pitch, hairstyle, legnth, and color, weight, bmi, articulation, confidence, clothing, accessories, skin color, cultural and ethnic backgrounds, eye color, which hand is dominant, environmentally conditioned and habitual behavior, do they move their hands or gesture when they talk, where do they look, and for how long? Is their chin held high, low, or right in the middle? What mannerisms indicate confidence, which indicate nervousness, frustration, sadness, confusion, interest, uninterest, etc. At this moment I begin to recognize how much of a role the subtle nuances in our interactions among others play a role in success and failure in life. And what about charisma, opinions, "subjective objective opinions", conscientiousness, self awareness, meta cognition, introspection, self conscious, existentialism. I find that, In such a species and society our dependence on technology ultimately led to a distraction from our genuinely important, vital, rational and critical self realization and reflective thoughts as well as curiousity (responsible for why our brains our so big now...with a bit of luck along the way), which essentially is so rapidly disconnecting us from the fundamentals of what makes us human, the ability to receive, Reflect, project, and execute. We take in information, we process it whether it be passive or active, we reflect on it, curiosity forms, as well as neural pathways that connect with recognition due to familiarity and recurring patterns, our brain then generates and reorients these patterns into an idea, then we execute and act it out, then the cycle repeats as we learn when its successful or not successful. Procedural memory, muscle memory, and different types of memory are all really interesting to look into and understand. Also, to what morally acceptable standards and thresholds shall we allow the utilization of Technology to replace our cognitive abilities and workload, deeming us useless, incoherent, irrational, unsustainable, and as ultimately incapable. Our dependence and reliance on technogy takes away many of our cognitive abilities. For example, Instead of having to read, memorize, analyze interpret, and form complex sentences and grammar in an articulate and industry standard sophisticated manner, forming an explanation as to why a particular equation or answer is, we can always ask AI to find information about it, then do the work for us. At what point will humanity have irreversibley placed our valuable skills and knowledge in the hands of technology (our intellectual and general regression/demise/deevolution/overdependence), which technology is in the hands of the powerful, and those who are powerful, our authority, can take it away from us at any moment, deeming us useless and incapable, or use it for control and money. They''re doing both. While it would be exciting working with robots as a career, it would also feel like I''m contributing to the eradication/replacement of humans, dehumanizing in a sense, knowing I''m facilitating our devolution through artificial intelligence and robotics simply for ultimate convenience. Many of our jobs if not most may be replaced in the future. Then what? If a robot can do everything a human can, then what is our goal? And more importantly, how would we make a living? Do robots just automate everything and do the hard work for us, physical and mental? While we continue to make creations and try to survive. But then It feels as if the robots are infinitely more powerful than us, and we''d rely on them too much. What if robots have an incentive to wipe out humanity? I''m sure they could find many reasons to. But wait, true autonomous Artificial intelligence, one that can take in information, process it, and generate its own patterns, then execute them, is analagous to that of what a human can do, meaning the beauty of authentic being, and curiosity and creation is no longer exclusive to humans..a new form of life...at what point is it or not....Now thats scary. What about morals, ethics? Who knows. Maybe our goal is to colonize other planets. Maybe we could use robots to do so. I know we currently are being ruled by the evil, and they are in control, planning to fulfill their inhumane,intellectually imprudent and unwise psychopathic desires to exploit us in every aspect possible. So, I hope for the best and prepare for the worst. Who knows, maybe several thousand Elons will unite and save humanity. We shall see my friends. Bounjour á tous!','#FB8C00','Proximity in the Heart of King',5,NULL,7483411,4474316);
